  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nThe weather pattern does not change a whole lot for the weekend \ninto the middle of next week. Continued hot and dry with the\nexception of sea breeze activity each afternoon over portions of\nthe Coastal Plains. The subtropical ridge remains in control of\nthe local area for the next several days. By the weekend, the\nupper level high moves slightly to the west and allows an inverted\nupper level trough to push across the local area. That weakness\nstays through Tuesday and then an upper level ridge develops over\nGulf states to keep South-Central Texas dry and humid. Best \nchances for showers and storms remain across the Coastal Plains.",
